  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "VPN path and how to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 4
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Source: senaev-media, Russia.** Each subscription profile has its own isolated Xray client. Only explicit test requests use its loopback SOCKS proxy; host traffic keeps its existing route.\n\n**Light checks:** direct + VPN HTTPS every ~30s. **Heavy checks:** direct/VPN exit IP and a capped 64 KiB download every ~5 min. Green requires a fresh successful sample; gaps mean no fresh samples. Scrape UP is exporter reachability, not tunnel health. Compare direct controls before attributing failures to VPN.\n\nThe download is rate-limited, not a speed benchmark. Actual exit IPs and failure details remain in Datadog logs.\n \n**Transfer matrix:** controlledExperiment keeps only profiles 1 and 4 active.\nRoutine/recovery panels have no new samples. Every matrix compares direct/VPN\n4, 16 and 64 KiB downloads from Cloudflare and HTTPBingo, with 60–90 quiet seconds\nbetween conditions and 300–360 quiet seconds between matrices. Order rotates.\nA failed small VPN precheck skips that transfer; check logs for skipped conditions,\ndirect_control_ok, cycle IDs and client-exit invalidation. Results cannot alone prove DPI.\n\n\n**XHTTP candidate (profile 4 only):** vpn = TCP/Reality; xhttp = XHTTP over verified TLS.\nBoth use senaev.com:443 and exit Hetzner. The candidate adds TLS termination/h2c proxying,\nso this compares complete setups, not transport alone. Variants run serially with\n60–90 quiet seconds between them and alternating order. Each round first validates\nthe candidate exit. Check logs for skipped candidates and invalidated cycles.\n\n\n**Response diagnostics:** after a failed candidate exit check, compare the same trace\ndirect/baseline, then small XHTTP requests and a separately reported 30s trace with\nquiet gaps. This never overrides the failed original 8s control. Info logs apply\nonly to the experimental client/backend. Set vpnXhttpExperiment.diagnostics=false\nto disable these additional requests and restore warning-level logging.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "title": "Reachable probe exporters",
      "type": "stat",
      "description": "Expected: two exporters in controlled experiment mode, four in routine mode. This is not VPN connectivity.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "P4169E866C3094E38"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "h": 4
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(up{job=\"vpn-probe\"})",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "P4169E866C3094E38"
